<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>Selecting someone on the Users page opens their profile, which has these tabs:</FluentText>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Details</strong>: first name, last name and phone number.</li>
        <li><strong>Password</strong>: set a new password for them (at least 6 characters).</li>
        <li><strong>Account</strong>: their status, <strong>Unlock Account</strong> if they're locked out, and
            <strong>Resend Invite</strong> or <strong>Send Password Reset Email</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>Documents</strong>: their staff documents, such as certificates and ID. Shown when your company
            has onboarding. See <a href="/help/onboarding?topic=documents">Onboarding help</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Rota</strong>: their positions, contract, time-off allowances, availability and clock-in PIN.
            Shown when your company has staff scheduling. See <a href="/help/rota?topic=setup">Rota help</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Danger Zone</strong>: <strong>Delete User</strong>. Admins also see
            <strong>Delete User Data (GDPR)</strong>.</li>
    </ul>

    <HelpNote Intent="MessageBarIntent.Warning">
        <strong>Delete User Data (GDPR)</strong> permanently removes the person's personal data and deletes
        their account. Things they wrote are kept but no longer show their name. It can't be undone, so only
        use it when someone asks for their data to be erased.
    </HelpNote>
</HelpTab>
